From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 1 Sep 2026 15:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] initializer: do not contact the OTA channel for pre-installed
 images

setup_config() queries the system and vendor OTA channels before it looks at
whether the images are already on disk, and only falls back to "None" after a
request fails. But http.retrieve() catches ValueError and HTTPError and nothing
else, so a DNS failure raises URLError, which propagates straight out and aborts
init:

  ERROR: <urlopen error [Errno -3] Temporary failure in name resolution>

That makes "waydroid init" impossible without a network on exactly the machines
that need no network, because their images are pre-installed. It also means a
machine deliberately pinned to a matched system/vendor pair has the channel pick
for it the moment it does have a network - which on a Halium host is how a
vendor image ends up paired with a system image several VNDK generations away.

Waydroid 1.6.3 returns early here for the same reasons. This restores that
behaviour on 1.4.2, where the channel lookup sits ahead of the vendor type
detection and setupBinderNodes(), so the block has to be guarded rather than
simply moved - returning early instead would skip binder setup and leave
args.BINDER_DRIVER unset.

Reproduced on tissot-halium and mindphone, both of which carry pre-installed
images and both of which failed to initialise until this was applied.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [fixed differently upstream in 1.6.3]
---
--- a/tools/actions/initializer.py
+++ b/tools/actions/initializer.py
@@ -47,44 +47,61 @@
         args.images_path = tools.config.defaults["images_path"]
     cfg["waydroid"]["images_path"] = args.images_path
 
-    channels_cfg = tools.config.load_channels()
-    if not args.system_channel:
-        args.system_channel = channels_cfg["channels"]["system_channel"]
-    if not args.vendor_channel:
-        args.vendor_channel = channels_cfg["channels"]["vendor_channel"]
-    if not args.rom_type:
-        args.rom_type = channels_cfg["channels"]["rom_type"]
-    if not args.system_type:
-        args.system_type = channels_cfg["channels"]["system_type"]
+    # Skip the OTA channel entirely when the images are already on disk.
+    #
+    # Contacting it first is not merely wasteful, it is fatal without DNS:
+    # http.retrieve() catches ValueError and HTTPError but not URLError, so a
+    # name resolution failure propagates out of setup_config and aborts
+    # "waydroid init" - on a machine whose images are sitting right there. It
+    # also means a machine pinned to a specific system/vendor pair can have the
+    # channel decide otherwise the moment it does have a network.
+    #
+    # 1.6.3 returns here for the same reason; this restores that behaviour on
+    # 1.4.2, whose ordering puts the channel lookup ahead of the vendor type and
+    # binder node setup, so the two cannot simply be swapped.
+    if args.images_path in preinstalled_images_paths:
+        args.system_ota = "None"
+        args.vendor_ota = "None"
+        args.vendor_type = get_vendor_type(args)
+    else:
+        channels_cfg = tools.config.load_channels()
+        if not args.system_channel:
+            args.system_channel = channels_cfg["channels"]["system_channel"]
+        if not args.vendor_channel:
+            args.vendor_channel = channels_cfg["channels"]["vendor_channel"]
+        if not args.rom_type:
+            args.rom_type = channels_cfg["channels"]["rom_type"]
+        if not args.system_type:
+            args.system_type = channels_cfg["channels"]["system_type"]
 
-    args.system_ota = args.system_channel + "/" + args.rom_type + \
-        "/waydroid_" + args.arch + "/" + args.system_type + ".json"
-    system_request = helpers.http.retrieve(args.system_ota)
-    if system_request[0] != 200:
-        if args.images_path not in preinstalled_images_paths:
-            raise ValueError(
-                "Failed to get system OTA channel: {}, error: {}".format(args.system_ota, system_request[0]))
-        else:
-            args.system_ota = "None"
+        args.system_ota = args.system_channel + "/" + args.rom_type + \
+            "/waydroid_" + args.arch + "/" + args.system_type + ".json"
+        system_request = helpers.http.retrieve(args.system_ota)
+        if system_request[0] != 200:
+            if args.images_path not in preinstalled_images_paths:
+                raise ValueError(
+                    "Failed to get system OTA channel: {}, error: {}".format(args.system_ota, system_request[0]))
+            else:
+                args.system_ota = "None"
 
-    device_codename = helpers.props.host_get(args, "ro.product.device")
-    args.vendor_type = None
-    for vendor in [device_codename, get_vendor_type(args)]:
-        vendor_ota = args.vendor_channel + "/waydroid_" + \
-            args.arch + "/" + vendor.replace(" ", "_") + ".json"
-        vendor_request = helpers.http.retrieve(vendor_ota)
-        if vendor_request[0] == 200:
-            args.vendor_type = vendor
-            args.vendor_ota = vendor_ota
-            break
+        device_codename = helpers.props.host_get(args, "ro.product.device")
+        args.vendor_type = None
+        for vendor in [device_codename, get_vendor_type(args)]:
+            vendor_ota = args.vendor_channel + "/waydroid_" + \
+                args.arch + "/" + vendor.replace(" ", "_") + ".json"
+            vendor_request = helpers.http.retrieve(vendor_ota)
+            if vendor_request[0] == 200:
+                args.vendor_type = vendor
+                args.vendor_ota = vendor_ota
+                break
 
-    if not args.vendor_type:
-        if args.images_path not in preinstalled_images_paths:
-            raise ValueError(
-                "Failed to get vendor OTA channel: {}".format(vendor_ota))
-        else:
-            args.vendor_ota = "None"
-            args.vendor_type = get_vendor_type(args)
+        if not args.vendor_type:
+            if args.images_path not in preinstalled_images_paths:
+                raise ValueError(
+                    "Failed to get vendor OTA channel: {}".format(vendor_ota))
+            else:
+                args.vendor_ota = "None"
+                args.vendor_type = get_vendor_type(args)
 
     if args.system_ota != cfg["waydroid"].get("system_ota"):
         cfg["waydroid"]["system_datetime"] = tools.config.defaults["system_datetime"]
